{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The bug was in `round_to_nickel` in `repo/pricing.py`:\n\n```6:7:/Users/psudokit/benchmark/runs/20260928-195603-g2-kimi-k3-T012-money-vague-prompt-r0/work/repo/pricing.py\ndef round_to_nickel(cents):\n    \"\"\"Round an integer cent amount to the nearest 5 cents.\n\n    23 cents rounds to 25, 22 cents rounds to 20.\n    \"\"\"\n    return ((cents + 2) // 5) * 5\n```\n\nIt was flooring to the multiple below (`(cents // 5) * 5`), so 23¢ showed as 20¢ instead of 25¢. Now it rounds to the nearest nickel (half-up), which flows through to `price_summary`'s `rounded_total` in `repo/rows.py` since it uses the same function. Both tests pass."}]},"session_id":"09a176e0-edd2-4b32-83ad-e1be7022c835"}
